<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Hodgson (superintendent)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Hodgson was a British officer sent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosquito-coast">Mosquito Coast</a> in 1740, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-jenkins-ear">War of Jenkins' Ear</a>, to win the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miskito">Miskito</a> as allies against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. He became the first British superintendent of the coast, and in 1749 a formal superintendency was established with its headquarters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-river-honduras">Black River</a> on the Honduran coast.</p></div>
